    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.06_topology_jepa.chapters.09_trace_outgoing_profile.sections.02_outgoing_profile_closure.concrete_anchor#overlapzone" .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_09_trace_outgoing_profile_sections_02_outgoing_profile_closure_concrete_anchor#overlapzone silm:hasLongDescription "The OverlapZone is the shared pixel region where the head patch and body patch both cover the neck-joint region of Mittens, requiring agreement on the apex glyph. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'U_overlap', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
